  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1001.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "2011-08-31",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1001.01 Purpose. The purpose of this part is to limit open air source pollution by regulating emissions of particulate matter and toxic air pollutants from the burning of materials where the products of combustion are discharged directly into the atmosphere rather than through a stack, chimney, or flue. Regulation of open burning is necessary to maintain attainment of the ambient air quality standards in accordance with sections 109 and 110 of the Clean Air Act, as amended, and to protect the public health and welfare pursuant to RSA 125-C:1.\n\nSource. #120, eff 8-31-73; ss by #721.1, eff 12-7-75; amd by #1036, eff 10-15-77; #1717, eff 2-19-81; ss by #2332, eff 4-29-83; ss by #2938, eff 12-27-84; ss by #5033, eff 12-27-90; ss by #6283-B, eff 7-10-96; ss by #7850, eff 3-12-03; ss by #9863, INTERIM, eff 3-4-11, EXPIRES: 8-31-11; ss by #9909, eff 5-1-11; ss by #12831, eff 8-1-19",
